.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string into a destination buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcpy
function copies the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.I dest
including the terminating null character.
.PP
The destination buffer must have enough space to store the copied string.
The function returns the number of characters copied, excluding the null terminator.
